  "slug": "entangled-microwaves-nonlinear-scattering-ed74",
  "summary": "Direct spectroscopic evidence of moiré-mediated coupling in graphene and graphene/hBN appears alongside metasurface studies of quasi-BIC and flatband tuning.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is moiré control of hybrid excitations in graphene-based systems. Twisted bilayer graphene, studied from AB stacking to 5.5°, hosts hyperbolic plasmon-phonon polaritons with gate-tunable wavelengths via remote moiré effects. In graphene/hBN superlattices, a Fano resonance is reported as the first direct observation of coupling between moiré flat-band electronic excitations and hBN out-of-plane optical phonons. Helicity-resolved Raman spectroscopy identifies reconfigurable chiral phonons in asymmetrically stacked moiré superlattices. Three metasurface works form a looser, parallel strand: THz collective flatbands with zero group velocity, polarization-independent strong coupling of Brillouin-zone-folding quasi-BICs with A excitons in WS2, and liquid-crystal tuning of anisotropy-induced quasi-BICs. The new element is direct spectroscopic evidence of moiré-mediated interlayer coupling alongside demonstrated tunability.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
